From 9acdfca7459db0129f9dfb799209efd8c7e31c6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: leow149 <leow149@lucidmail.xyz>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:03:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 43/45] wifi: xradio: Add XR829 support (WIP: scanning works)

The XR829 (SDIO 0a9e:2282) runs a newer firmware ("HT40" API) that uses
16-bit rate entries (modem type, bandwidth, flags, rate index) instead of
8-bit rate indices. Select it at runtime from the SDIO ID:
- firmware files xr829/{boot,fw,sdd}_xr829.bin, DPLL sync with the BT core
- start scan: scan type in the flags byte, rate entry
- template frames: 8-byte header with a rate entry
- receive indication: rate entry + 3 reserved bytes; map back to the old
  rate index, report 40 MHz / short GI

Also fixes: HT frames were flagged RX_ENC_HT in hdr->flag (= MMIC error)
instead of hdr->encoding; a cached RX skb was reused without resetting its
data pointer (skb_over_panic on a 520-byte frame); a WARN on debug-only
message names.

Not done yet: join, TX rate policy, TX, AP mode.

Signed-off-by: leow149 <leow149@lucidmail.xyz>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
